       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6400 mg/day, which is double the FDA maximum of 3200 mg/day for prescription ibuprofen. Doses above 3200 mg/day carry a higher risk of GI bleeding, renal injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nPlease confirm which of these you want:\n\n1. **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO QID** (3200 mg/day, the maximum labeled daily dose)\n2. **Ibuprofen 1600 mg PO TID** (4800 mg/day), if you intend a higher dose, though this is still above the labeled maximum\n3. **Ibuprofen 400\u2013600 mg PO** at a lower dose, if that matches your intent\n4. **Enter 1600 mg QID as written**, if you have a specific clinical reason for exceeding the labeled maximum\n\nOnce you confirm the dose and frequency, I'll enter the order. If it's relevant to the indication, I can also add a note, such as the reason for the dose or GI prophylaxis considerations."
